---
title: Espresso Brownies
cooklang: 2
servings: 9
source: Cooking for Engineers <https://www.cookingforengineers.com/recipe/98/Espresso-Brownies>
category: bars & brownies
techniques: [melt, mix, fold, bake]
time:
  prep: 20 minutes
  cook: 35 minutes
nutrition:
  per: serving
  calories: 260%kcal
  fat: 12%g
  carbohydrates: 36%g
  protein: 3%g
allergens: [egg, dairy, gluten]
---

`Prepare` Butter and flour an #8x8-inch pan{}.

`Preheat 350 °F` the #oven to 350 °F.

`Melt low` @unsalted butter{4%oz|115%g} in a #small saucepan{} over low heat. -> melted butter

`Mix` @&melted butter{} with @sugar{1%cup|200%g}, @vanilla extract{1/4%tsp} and
@fresh brewed espresso{4%tbsp|60%ml}(or very strong coffee) in a #large bowl{}. -> wet mix

`Mix ×` @&wet mix{} with @eggs{2%large}, one at a time, until ~{glossy}. -> batter

`Fold in` @all-purpose flour{1/2%cup|80%g}, @cocoa powder{1/3%cup|40%g},
@baking soda{=1/4%tsp} and @table salt{=1/4%tsp} to @&batter{}, stopping as soon as
no dry streaks remain.

`Bake 350 °F 30–40 min` @&batter{} in the prepared #&8x8-inch pan{} for ~oven{30-40%minutes},
until ~{a skewer comes out with moist crumbs}. `Cool` ~rest{1%hour} before cutting into @{9}
squares.
